            "comparator:post-marginal"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "notices": [],
      "changes": [
        "Independently formalize one global normalized typical vector selected from the original actual X marginal, its canonical-coordinate action, norm, actual selected X marginal, and the actual marginal positive-semidefinite and entropy bounds simultaneously on every physical region disjoint from X. Canonical coordinate and marginal identities are proved internally; the selected vector never depends on the observed region. No supplied coordinate or marginal certificate, full-rank hypothesis, enlarged-region spectral assumption, or assumed entropy bound is used."
      ],
      "no_upstream_proof_text_reused": true,
      "verification": {
